0result.sql is the best choice because:  
• It uses Snowflake‑supported functions only (YEAR, COALESCE, ROUND).  
• The GROUP BY expression matches the SELECT expression, so the query compiles.  
• The date filter (`YEAR("DATE_OF_LOSS") BETWEEN 2010 AND 2019`) cleanly limits rows to the requested range.  
• It avoids alias‑in‑GROUP BY issues found in 1result.sql and is simpler than the extra CAST/ROUND layering in 2result.sql.

